## What we heard

Over 10 weeks, more than 1,400 state employees told us how they’d make government more efficient.

 
----
id: overview
----

## A government that works better starts with the people who know it best

We asked for people’s insights, both as Californians and as state employees. Our state employees are experts on how our government serves its residents. They are also Californians who use public services. We value their experience from both sides.

Our goals:
- Identify barriers to an efficient and effective government
- Discover opportunities to better serve the people in our state


----
id: about
----

### About the process

Engaged California is more than a suggestion box. It’s a collaborative platform where people can share, refine, and rank ideas that drive change.

This is a model of deliberative democracy. It gives you a meaningful role in shaping government services in California.

When you take part, you help us listen better, work smarter, and deliver more for the people we serve.

[Learn more about Engaged California](/about)

